name    mod-kill-collector: a relog keeps the collection, full bags mail the token, reload keeps the progress
# Server-side test bot run (mod-fl-testbots), T1.
# 1. A first Snapjaw (2408) pays a token; after a relog the collection is read back from the database, so a
#    second Snapjaw still pays nothing.
# 2. `.killcollector reload` rebuilds the lists and recomputes the online collections: the count stays.
# 3. With full bags (the director fills them with Worn Shortswords, 25, which do not stack) the token of the
#    next first kill (a Gray Bear, 2351, by the river) arrives by mail: the bags hold no token. The mail itself is
#    checked in the characters database after the run.
# The kills are three triggered Arcane Explosions (42921), as in kill_collector_tokens, at other Snapjaw spawns
# (a corpse from that scenario's run would still lie at its places).
# Each creature is respawned by the director (`.respawn` on the picked one, which replaces the object, so
# it is picked again) before its kill: the scenario runs again while an earlier run's corpse still lies there.
timeout 240s

bot a mage
group party

place 0 -10.3 -1111.9 36.1
require a alive
do gm target a
as gm .killcollector reset
expect output has "collection reset"
do a destroy 920200
do a destroy 25

log 1 - a relog keeps the collection
pick t1 creature:2408 near a
do gm target t1
as gm .respawn
wait 1s
pick t1 creature:2408 near a
require t1 alive
do a approach t1
wait 1s
do a cast 42921 triggered
do a cast 42921 triggered
do a cast 42921 triggered
waitfor t1 dead timeout 5s
wait 2s
expect a item 920200 == 1
do a relog
waitfor a exists timeout 30s
wait 2s
as a .killcollector status
expect output has "1 different creatures killed"
place 0 38.7 -1118.6 35.1
pick t2 creature:2408 near a
do gm target t2
as gm .respawn
wait 1s
pick t2 creature:2408 near a
require t2 alive
do a approach t2
wait 1s
do a cast 42921 triggered
do a cast 42921 triggered
do a cast 42921 triggered
waitfor t2 dead timeout 5s
wait 1s
expect a item 920200 == 1

log 2 - reload keeps the progress
as gm .killcollector reload
expect output has "rebuilt"
as a .killcollector status
expect output has "1 different creatures killed"

log 3 - full bags: the token comes by mail (no token stack in the bags either, so nothing can merge)
do a destroy 920200
# .additem reads a bare number first as a character guid, so the bot is named (slot 1 mage = Tbmaga)
as gm .additem Tbmaga 25 200
place 0 -92.2 -1117.3 44.9
pick g1 creature:2351 near a
do gm target g1
as gm .respawn
wait 1s
pick g1 creature:2351 near a
require g1 alive
do a approach g1
wait 1s
do a cast 42921 triggered
do a cast 42921 triggered
do a cast 42921 triggered
waitfor g1 dead timeout 5s
wait 1s
expect a item 920200 == 0
as a .killcollector status
expect output has "2 different creatures killed"

cleanup
do a destroy 25
do a destroy 920200
log kill collector edges done
